<title>USA: Quaker Chemical sells Euro pulp business.</title>
<headline>Quaker Chemical sells Euro pulp business.</headline>
<dateline>CONSHOHOCKEN, Pa. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quaker Chemical Corp said Tuesday that Veba Textilni Zavody A.S.'s Servo Delden will buy its European pulp and paper business for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to see a second quarter non-recurring gain of $0.21 per share from the sale.</p>
<p>Quaker Chemical said the pulp and paper business in Europe was a small percentage of its total sales, and the defoamers and pulp dispersants it sold were no longer considered core products in the United States. The deal will not affect the Quaker Chemical's North American pulp and paper business.</p>
</text>
